WEBVTT

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.530
Scotch eggs, please.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.110
I would like one hard-boiled, 
and the other soft-boiled.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.870
That will be served with bread.
 Is that acceptable?

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:40.920
Yes.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.870
The same for you, Master Emilio?

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:46.250
Yes... I'll leave it to you.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:50.590
And please prepare twenty 
more to go, as well.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:51.440
Very well.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.480
You usually bring your 
grandchildren with you.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:03.420
It's unusual to see you 
bringing a human girl.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.720
Aletta, this is...

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:07.580
I'm...

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:09.370
I'm...

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.110
a boy!

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.700
What?!

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:19.000
<i>It was only a few hours ago that 
I found out I was coming to Nekoya.</i>

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.870
<b>The Southern Continent</b>

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.610
<i>I had left my hometown to go on a journey.</i>

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.450
<i>I wanted to become stronger.</i>

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.410
<i>Because I've always looked like this...</i>

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.340
I love you.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.840
Please, no!

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.590
Marry me.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.250
But I'm a boy!

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.960
<i>I thought those things would stop 
happening if I got stronger.</i>

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.140
<i>I cut off my hair</i>

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.990
<i>and put on the strongest-looking 
clothes I could find.</i>

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.390
<i>But it didn't work.</i>

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.290
<i>I thought I could get stronger 
if I went on a journey,</i>

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.980
<i>but I still haven't gained 
any stamina or muscle.</i>

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:06.290
The last time I ate was two nights ago.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.290
It's no use.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.160
I can't...

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:17.130
Are you awake now?

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.080
Where am I?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.160
Oh, dear. It appears I've startled you.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.800
I'm terribly sorry.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.520
Uh, it's okay.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.330
Are you... a lamia?

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.240
Yes. My name is Lucia.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:39.260
I found you unconscious in the forest,

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.460
and brought you here to take care of you.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.030
I'm Emilio.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.080
Thank you for your help.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:51.810
And what brought you so 
close to a lamia settlement?

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.650
I was on a journey to get stronger,

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.560
and I...

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.630
I'm sorry.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.170
So you passed out because you were hungry?

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.930
Would you like to have a meal with me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.960
What? Really?

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.140
Of course.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.670
Today is a special day.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.320
I will treat you.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.300
There's a new face.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.320
How beautiful.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.780
I wonder where they're going.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.850
Where else could it be? 
Today is the Day of Satur.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.790
Please do not be offended.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.360
Visitors very rarely come here,

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:37.080
so they can't help being curious about you.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.540
Oh...

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.360
We're eating here?

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.250
Yes.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:52.590
Lumia...

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.440
Oh, Grandmother. What brings you here?

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.930
Grandmother?!

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.440
Is something wrong?

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.940
Uh, no... nothing at all.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.050
I believe today was your day to go to Nekoya,

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:10.850
but would you mind letting 
this visitor have your turn?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.390
No, I don't mind.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:14.620
Thank you.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.050
But in return,

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:19.510
I'd appreciate it if you could bring a 
large quantity of one item back for me.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:20.590
All right.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.420
Um... What is "Nekoya"?

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.670
The place we are heading to.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.680
What's a door doing here?

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:42.130
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.800
Come, let us go.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:44.870
<i>And now, here I am.</i>

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.330
Do you find something strange?

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.270
Yes... There are quite a few 
unusual-looking people here.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.450
All the furnishings are so different, too.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.840
We are in another world.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.990
And they are all people who 
came here from our world

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:11.710
through a door much like the one we took.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.100
Another world?

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:19.140
Well, it appears our food was 
finished while we were talking.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:25.440
<i>Scotch Egg</i>

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:23.340
Thank you for waiting. 
Here are your Scotch eggs.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.440
Wow! They look delicious!

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.300
Please enjoy your meal.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.990
We will. Thank you.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.630
Pardon me.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.050
Well, shall we eat?

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.080
Yes!

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:38.720
What kind of bread is this?

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:42.240
It's made with something called 
"wheat," a type of grass seed.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.120
"Wheat," huh?

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:49.000
It smells so nice.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.370
This is delicious!

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:58.270
The taste and texture are nothing 
like the food I normally eat!

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.100
Yes, the bread is lovely,

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.100
but please try the Scotch eggs, too.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.060
Okay, then...

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.450
<i>The crispy, flavorful breading,</i>

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:22.880
<i>the meat and oranie seasoned 
with salt and spices,</i>

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.130
<i>the egg boiled to the perfect hardness...</i>

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:31.130
<i>The more I chew it, the more the flavors 
mix together as one in my mouth.</i>

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:32.520
Do you like it?

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.330
Yes! It's delicious!

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:35.560
Isn't it?

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:39.890
But that's not the only 
way to enjoy Scotch eggs.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.650
Next, try putting some of 
this red "chili sauce" on it.

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:00.330
<i>Ah, that's spicy!</i>

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.490
<i>It's spicy, but it has a sourness to it, too.</i>

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:07.510
<i>Is this a marmett sauce with togaran in it?</i>

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:12.170
<i>Adding the spiciness and 
sourness of the chili sauce</i>

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.760
<i>makes the meat and egg taste even better!</i>

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.470
I'm so glad you seem to enjoy it.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.020
Now it's time for the soft-boiled one.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.360
Soft-boiled?

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:27.150
Why didn't they cut this one?

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.960
You'll see when you cut it yourself.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.030
Whoa! The yolk!

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:38.780
That's right. The yolk is still 
runny in a soft-boiled egg.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.550
Please, go ahead and try it.

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.370
Okay...

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.470
<i>The viscous texture of the yolk</i>

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.070
<i>gives it a richness that the 
hard-boiled one didn't have!</i>

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:57.670
<i>It's almost like a sauce 
made to go with the meat!</i>

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.290
<i>And it softens the spiciness</i>

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.560
<i>of the chili sauce, making it a great match!</i>

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:22.120
They were both incredibly delicious.

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:25.260
I'm so glad you liked them.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.400
Which was your favorite?

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:33.120
It's so hard to choose...

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:40.970
Now, Master Emilio, you said 
you were on a journey, yes?

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:41.850
Yes.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:46.890
Would you be interested in training under me?

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.520
What? Training?

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:51.650
I am, in fact, quite strong.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.650
So strong that I can assume 
the form of a dragon.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:55.780
A dragon?!

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.170
Yes. I'm sure I can help 
you grow stronger, too.

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:01.350
Stronger...

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:09.290
Please allow me to train under you!

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:13.290
In that case, I look forward 
to working with you.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:13.980
Me, too!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:17.030
Shall we take our leave now?

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.530
Thank you for waiting. 
Here are your Scotch eggs to go.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:27.810
It was truly delicious, as always.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.690
Thank you very much.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.190
Um... Emilio-san!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.940
I'm, uh... very sorry about what I said!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.440
Oh, no...

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:41.570
I'm sorry for raising my voice, too.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.310
Please come see us again sometime.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:45.040
I will!

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.480
Well, until next time.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.470
Welcome back, Lady Lucia!

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:02.480
Master Emilio...

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.410
My training will be quite rigorous.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.380
You had best prepare yourself.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:09.160
Okay!

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:13.980
Then, first, please hand out these 
Scotch eggs to all of these ladies.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:15.340
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:20.270
I truly look forward to working with you.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:21.180
Me, too!

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:40.970
Hey, morning.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.140
Morning.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:43.960
I'll stick these in the fridge.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.520
Thanks for always bringing them.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:48.220
No problem.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.210
There, all done.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:59.480
The ol' bones start to feel a 
little rickety at our age, huh?

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:02.110
Yeah. Want some tea before you go?

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.110
Nah, I'll pass.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.390
I haven't finished prepping the shop yet.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.120
Oh, okay.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.810
Oh, by the way, has the old lady who 
gets the mont blanc been here lately?

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:12.500
No...

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.500
I heard she passed away.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.000
Really?

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:20.420
Though... I wouldn't call 
him her replacement, but...

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:26.930
Mr. Thomas, I would like you to search 
for a certain dessert made with marone.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.490
Will you do that for me?

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:32.150
You can find all kinds of 
marone desserts right in town.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:36.710
I am offering a reward of 3,000 silver coins.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.440
<i>Three thousand</i> silver coins?!

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.190
That's just how valuable this dessert is.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:44.510
You don't say...

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:50.700
The head maid, Jazelle, used 
to buy them from somewhere,

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.750
but she fell ill about a month ago, and...

00:12:54.310 --> 00:13:00.260
She would serve that dessert, 
"mont blanc," to special guests.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:05.030
It became famous as a dessert 
that could only be found here.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.610
Many came here in search of it specifically.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:13.330
I get it. If you can't serve 
something you used to serve...

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:16.200
That's a good way for a leader 
to lose the people's trust.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.190
Yes.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.190
I'll accept the job.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:26.610
I'll find this "mont blanc" 
stuff for you. Just you watch!

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:33.200
That's what I told her, 
but I can't find any leads at all.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:40.710
No one else ever knew how that head 
maid got her hands on the mont blanc.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:46.090
What kind of place can an old lady get 
in and out of without anyone noticing?

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:47.910
It couldn't be...

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.850
inside the mansion, could it?!

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:56.930
The head maid brought mont blanc 
here once every seven days.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:58.310
That's right.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:02.810
Lady Eleanor asked her a few 
times to buy it on other days,

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.240
but she wouldn't do it.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:08.880
Did she do anything differently 
on that one day out of seven?

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:11.870
Hmm, I'm not sure...

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.480
Oh, come to think of it,

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:18.300
there's a room where Lady Eleanor's dresses 
and toys from her childhood are stored.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:19.800
She always went in there.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:22.500
I think today is that one 
day out of seven, isn't it?

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.960
Damn...

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:29.020
I really thought it smelled like a lead.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:34.720
But I can't find anything 
out of the ordinary.

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:37.350
I guess I was off the mark.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.940
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.940
What the heck is this?!

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.660
Could it be...

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:49.360
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:52.160
that the source of her mont 
blanc is through this door?!

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:02.460
Welcome!

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.490
Please take a seat wherever you'd like.

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.130
What is this place?

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:14.220
Um...

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.490
Are you all right?

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:18.270
Oh, er, pardon me.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:23.110
Uh... just what is this place?

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.980
It's an eatery called Nekoya.

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:27.440
A restaurant?

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:31.990
Hey, miss! Did an old lady 
named Jazelle ever come here?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.870
Yes! You know Jazelle-san?

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:38.680
Do you sell a dessert 
called "mont blanc" here?!

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.410
Yes, we do.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.880
<i>This is the place!</i>

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:46.020
I'd like one order of the mont blanc.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:46.800
Sure!

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:52.930
<i>Since I found it, I might as well eat 
this dessert that's worth 3,000 silver.</i>

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.300
Would you like black tea with that?

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.680
There's a discount if 
you order them together.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:59.870
Black tea?

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:04.360
It's a drink with a lovely aroma 
that goes well with sweets.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.510
Ah, then I'll take that, too.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.120
Coming right up!

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:10.940
Hey, Aletta!

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.880
While you're at it, could I get 
another order of minced meat cutlets?

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:14.890
Sure!

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:19.200
<i>She did say this was an eatery,</i>

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:23.630
<i>but it's bizarre to see so many 
different races in one place.</i>

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:28.830
<i>Who would've expected to find a 
place like this inside a closet?</i>

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:30.740
This your first time here?

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:35.590
Yeah... What is this place, exactly?

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.420
It's Nekoya,

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:41.020
a restaurant that serves cuisine from 
another world once every seven days.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:43.680
Everyone calls it the 
Restaurant to Another World.

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.470
Another world?

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:47.810
You mean this is a different world?!

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:48.270
Yep.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:53.970
Then... does the door leading to this 
"Nekoya" place pop up in different locations?!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.030
It sure does.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:58.500
Abandoned mines, caves, deep in forests...

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.290
It shows up in all kinds of places.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.800
I see...

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.450
Hey, are you in the same line of work as me?

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.790
What line of work?

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:09.170
You're a treasure hunter, aren't you?

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:11.730
I figured you were from the aura about you.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:15.180
Oh, I've already retired, actually.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.080
My eyes aren't as sharp as they used to be.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.650
Oh, that's too bad.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:22.310
If you were still in the business, 
we could've shared information.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.820
Sorry I couldn't meet your expectations.

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:28.360
But if you wanna hear old stories, 
I'll tell you some next time.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.810
What's your name?

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:33.320
My name is... Minced Meat Cutlet.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:37.510
Isn't that the name of the 
dish you just ordered?

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:41.530
We all call each other by the 
names of our favorite dishes here.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:45.210
<i>Mont Blanc</i>

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.210
Thank you for waiting. 
Here's your mont blanc.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:49.310
Feel free to add sugar to the black 
tea if you prefer it that way.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.830
This is mont blanc?

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:55.590
It has a pretty weird shape.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.870
Well, guess I'll try it.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.410
<i>What is this?!</i>

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:10.470
<i>The marone's been boiled to the point that 
it's sweet all the way to the center?!</i>

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:14.360
<i>It doesn't even compare to the 
roasted chestnuts we have with tea!</i>

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.360
<i>This is making me excited 
to try the bottom part!</i>

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:22.610
<i>The whole thing is covered 
with marone... threads?</i>

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:26.160
<i>Did they crush the marone 
and mix it with sugar?!</i>

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:30.000
<i>It falls apart in my mouth 
and melts right away!</i>

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.750
<i>The milk is so soft, smooth, and just
 the right level of sweetness!</i>

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:40.260
<i>And this fluffy bread-like part that 
tastes like eggs is so sweet and tasty!</i>

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:45.410
<i>Every individual component is exquisite 
enough to be a taste fit for nobility,</i>

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:49.640
<i>and they've put them all together 
in a single indulgent dessert!</i>

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:56.400
<i>Mont blanc... What a luxurious 
dessert you are.</i>

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:59.530
Hey, you! The young lady with the black hair!

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:03.510
Thank you for waiting.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:07.630
Whoa! I heard a voice speaking 
directly into my head!

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:09.540
Was that your voice?

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.970
Do you always talk to people like that?

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:16.300
Yes. I sincerely apologize if I startled you.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.990
Nah, I don't mind.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.540
I want another order of this mont blanc.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:22.510
Your order has been accepted.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.810
<i>This black tea stuff is good, too!</i>

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:31.160
<i>It calms the sweetness of the mont blanc</i>

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:33.690
<i>and fills my mouth with 
the aroma of tea leaves.</i>

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.440
<i>When I took this job,</i>

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:40.910
<i>I thought she was crazy to offer 3,000 
silver for one little dessert.</i>

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:44.270
<i>But now that I know how 
good it is, I understand.</i>

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:56.380
Whew, I really pigged out.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.960
Ah, excuse me.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.170
Yes? What can I do for you?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.960
I'd like six mont blanc to take back with me.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:06.010
Of course. I'll get them ready right away.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:11.280
I gotta thank that head maid of theirs.

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:15.440
Thank you very much!

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.670
See you next time, Mont Blanc-san.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:27.470
Yeah, next time, Minced Meat Cutlet.

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.430
Thank you for waiting.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:36.210
Oh, thanks a lot.

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:39.720
Sir, I hear you were 
acquainted with Jazelle-san?

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:41.710
Oh... Yeah, something like that.

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:45.840
I haven't seen her in some 
time. Is she all right?

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:47.110
Uh...

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:49.850
She passed away due to an illness.

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.890
I see...

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:55.610
By the way, are you the owner of this place?

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:57.980
Huh? Yes, I am.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:00.800
So that means you make the food, right?

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:01.440
Yes...

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:05.240
You are incredible! I can't believe 
you can make such a tasty dessert!

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:08.480
Uh, actually, I didn't 
make that. It's from—

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.670
I've never eaten anything like that before!

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:13.870
It was <i>seriously</i> good!

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.570
Well, bye!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.320
Thank you very much.

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:29.880
<i>Well, I found where they come from.</i>

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:33.140
<i>It's a shame I won't be able 
to eat any more mont blanc now.</i>

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:35.350
<i>But according to Minced Meat Cutlet,</i>

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:39.560
<i>there are at least enough doors scattered 
around to let all those customers in.</i>

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:44.050
<i>Maybe I'll hold off on reporting back 
on this job until I find another door.</i>

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:49.320
Oh, so someone who knew her comes instead?

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:53.660
And he has the mistaken idea 
that I make the mont blanc.

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:56.360
Not that you mind, right?

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:58.270
Well, I kind of feel bad.

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.960
Oh, I stayed longer than I meant to.

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:01.790
See ya.

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:04.920
Yep. Thanks again.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:42.480
<i>Rice Burger</i>

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Pizza</i>
